---
import Page from '../../layouts/Page.astro'
import {
	IS_DRAFT,
	OPERATOR,
	TERMS_DATE_LABEL,
	TERMS_VERSION,
	VENUE,
	WEBAPP_HOST,
	WEBSITE_HOST,
	field,
} from '../../legal'

/**
 * Английская оферта — перевод русского оригинала, а не самостоятельный документ.
 *
 * Юрист вычитывал русскую версию, поэтому здесь прямо сказано, что при расхождении
 * приоритет за ней. Любая правка по существу вносится в обе страницы сразу.
 */
---

<Page
	title="Terms of Service — Between Bubbles"
	description="Terms of use for the Between Bubbles service."
	noindex={IS_DRAFT}
	longform
	lang="en"
	alternatePath="/offer"
>
	<p class="eyebrow">Legal</p>
	<h1>Terms of Service</h1>
	<p class="version">Last updated: {TERMS_DATE_LABEL.en} · Version: {TERMS_VERSION}</p>

	{
		IS_DRAFT && (
			<div class="notice">
				<p style="margin: 0">
					<strong>Draft.</strong> The text describes the service as it actually works, but
					the rightholder's details have not been confirmed yet and are shown in square
					brackets. Until they are filled in and the text is reviewed by a lawyer, this
					document is not a public offer.
				</p>
			</div>
		)
	}

	<div class="notice">
		<p style="margin: 0">
			This is a translation of the Russian original. In case of any discrepancy between the
			two versions, the <a href="/offer">Russian version</a> prevails.
		</p>
	</div>

	<h2>1. Parties and Subject Matter</h2>
	<p>
		This document is a public offer by {field(OPERATOR.name.en, 'operator name')} (hereinafter —
		the Rightholder), addressed to any legally capable adult individual (hereinafter — the
		User), to enter into an agreement on the use of the Between Bubbles service on the terms
		set out below.
	</p>
	<p>
		The service is the Between Bubbles web application: a personal wine tasting diary
		available at {WEBSITE_HOST} and {WEBAPP_HOST}. The service is intended for personal,
		non-commercial use: keeping track of what the User has tasted and of their own
		impressions.
	</p>

	<h2>2. Conclusion of the Agreement</h2>
	<p>
		The agreement is considered concluded at the moment the User, during registration, ticks
		the consent checkbox for these terms and the privacy policy and creates an account. The
		service records the date of consent and the document version in effect at that moment.
		No separate signing on paper is required.
	</p>

	<h2>3. Age Restriction</h2>
	<p>
		The service is available only to individuals who have reached 18 years of age. The date of
		birth is requested during registration; providing false information is grounds for
		blocking the account. Excessive alcohol consumption is harmful to your health. The service
		does not provide medical advice, does not encourage consumption, and is not an
		advertisement for alcoholic beverages.
	</p>

	<h2>4. What the User Receives</h2>
	<p>
		The Rightholder grants the right to use the service for its intended purpose: to keep
		tasting entries, store photos, maintain a personal wine directory, view weekly metrics and
		statistics, export their data, and publish individual entries via a link. This right is
		not transferable to third parties.
	</p>
	<p>
		The service is currently provided free of charge. The set of features may change and
		expand. If paid features appear, their terms will be published in advance as a separate
		document; the export of data already created remains available in any case.
	</p>

	<h2>5. Account</h2>
	<ul>
		<li>
			The password and access to the email account are the User's responsibility. Actions
			performed under the account are considered performed by the User.
		</li>
		<li>
			If you suspect your account has been compromised, change the password: doing so revokes
			all active sessions on all devices.
		</li>
		<li>
			The email address is used for service messages: address confirmation, password
			recovery, and notifications about changes to these terms. The service does not send
			marketing emails.
		</li>
	</ul>

	<h2>6. User Data and Content</h2>
	<ul>
		<li>
			Entries, wine cards, notes, and photos remain yours. The Rightholder acquires no rights
			to them beyond those technically necessary to operate the service: to store, process,
			display them to you, include them in your export, and in a publication you created
			yourself.
		</li>
		<li>
			The User confirms that they are entitled to upload these photos and texts and that
			these do not infringe the rights of third parties.
		</li>
		<li>
			It is prohibited to upload other people's personal data, unlawful materials, insults,
			or advertising.
		</li>
		<li>
			Store names enter a shared directory and become available to other Users when selecting
			a store; the link between a name and its author is not shown in the interface and is
			erased together with the account.
		</li>
	</ul>

	<h2>7. Publishing an Entry via a Link</h2>
	<ul>
		<li>
			A link is created only by the User's action. The address consists of 16 random
			characters and cannot be found by brute force.
		</li>
		<li>
			The publication includes photos, the wine and its characteristics, the rating, taste
			category, impressions, and notes, as well as the User's name — if they enabled that
			toggle. Price, store, email address, and other entries are not included.
		</li>
		<li>
			The link can be revoked in one click, after which the page stops opening. Copies,
			screenshots, and messenger caches made while the link was active are outside the
			Rightholder's control.
		</li>
		<li>A published page is closed to indexing by search engines.</li>
	</ul>

	<h2>8. Usage Restrictions</h2>
	<p>
		The following is not permitted: interfering with the operation of the service, bypassing
		rate limits, collecting data by automated means, attempting to gain access to other users'
		diaries, probing security without the Rightholder's written permission, and using the
		service for unlawful purposes or to promote alcoholic beverages.
	</p>

	<h2>9. Service Availability</h2>
	<p>
		The service is provided "as is". The Rightholder does not guarantee uninterrupted
		operation or the absence of errors: scheduled maintenance, updates, and outages caused by
		providers are possible. Database backups are made regularly; nevertheless, the User is
		advised to keep their own export — it is available in the settings in CSV and JSON formats
		at any time.
	</p>

	<h2>10. Liability</h2>
	<p>
		The service is a personal record-keeping tool, not medical, dietary, or other professional
		advice. Decisions about alcohol consumption are made by the User independently and at
		their own responsibility. To the extent permitted by applicable law, the Rightholder is
		not liable for lost profits or indirect damages arising from the use of, or inability to
		use, the service.
	</p>

	<h2>11. Termination</h2>
	<ul>
		<li>
			The User may delete their account in the settings at any time. Deletion is soft: for 30
			days recovery upon request remains possible, after which the data is deleted
			irreversibly.
		</li>
		<li>
			The Rightholder may suspend or terminate access in the event of a breach of these
			terms, a false date of birth, a threat to the operability or security of the service,
			and in cases provided for by law. Where possible, with prior notice by email.
		</li>
		<li>
			If the service is discontinued entirely, the Rightholder will notify Users at least 30
			days in advance and will keep data export available until that date.
		</li>
	</ul>

	<h2>12. Changes to the Terms</h2>
	<p>
		A new version is published on this page with a new date and version number. The Rightholder
		notifies Users of material changes at the email address provided during registration and,
		where necessary, requests consent again. Continued use of the service after a new version
		takes effect constitutes agreement with it.
	</p>

	<h2>13. Governing Law and Disputes</h2>
	<p>
		This agreement is governed by the law of {field(VENUE.jurisdiction.en, 'governing law country')}.
		The parties resolve disputes by correspondence: a request is sent to
		{' '}<a href={`mailto:${OPERATOR.email}`}>{field(OPERATOR.email, 'contact email address')}</a>,
		with a response time of 30 days. Unresolved disputes are considered by
		{' '}{field(VENUE.disputeVenue.en, 'dispute venue')}.
	</p>

	<h2>14. Rightholder Details</h2>
	<ul>
		<li>Name: {field(OPERATOR.name.en, 'operator name')}</li>
		<li>Registration: Tax ID {field(OPERATOR.registration, 'operator tax id')}</li>
		<li>Address: {field(OPERATOR.address.en, 'operator address')}</li>
		<li>
			Email: <a href={`mailto:${OPERATOR.email}`}>{field(OPERATOR.email, 'contact email address')}</a>
		</li>
	</ul>
</Page>
